DESCRIPTION:Friday\, April 10\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museu
 m of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 48m\n\n1960 | 108 min. | South Korea |
  Black-and-White | Korean with English subtitles | DCP \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN 
 BY: Kim Ki-young \nWITH: Kim Jin-kyu\, Ju Jeung-nyeo\, Lee Eun-shim\, Um A
 eng-ran \nThe Housemaid was restored in 2008 by the Korean Film Archive (K
 OFA)\, in association with The Film Foundation’s World Cinema Project an
 d HFR-Digital Film laboratory. Additional restoration funded by Armani\, C
 artier\, Qatar Airways\, and Qatar Museum Authority.\n\nType: Screenings\n
 \nRadical and uncompromising\, Kim Ki-young’s Housemaid trilogy starts i
 n 1960 with a first chapter that continues to influence new generations of
  filmmakers more than 60 years later. A deep survey on desire\, obsession\
 , and ego-driven revenge\, this domestic horror film follows a bourgeois f
 amily who hires Myung-sook (Lee Eun-shim)\, an unsophisticated young woman
 \, as their housemaid. When she becomes smitten with patriarch Dong-sik Ki
 m\, a series of strange episodes unfold\, and Myung-sook’s catastrophic 
 infatuation threatens the family bond. Kim’s unconventional language of 
 cinema depicts a bleak reality that is borderline ludicrous\, in an unconv
 entional blend of genres that redefined filmmaking in Korea.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-housemaid-019be23
 7-abf6-a8bd-0d36-f893ba7926ab
