BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:'Round Midnight in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260415T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260415T223000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019be20f-3f2a-ec78-e260-05875ed0f9d5@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Selected by the Music Branch\n\nWednesday\, April 15\, 2026 at
  7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 13m
 \n\n1986 | 133 min. | France | Color | French\, English | Rated R | 4K DCP
  \nDIRECTED BY: Bertrand Tavernier \nWRITTEN BY: David Rayfiel\, Bertrand 
 Tavernier \nWITH: Dexter Gordon\, Francois Cluzet\, Sandra Reaves-Phillips
 \, Martin Scorsese\n\nType: Screenings\n\nInternationally acclaimed filmma
 ker Bertrand Tavernier (Safe Conduct\, 2002) expressed his life-long love 
 of jazz with this heartfelt musical drama set in 1950s Paris. French star 
 Francois Cluzet (The Intouchables\, 2011) plays a young music fan who befr
 iends a troubled saxophone player portrayed by real-life musician Dexter G
 ordon\, who earned a Best Actor nomination for his subtle\, lived-in perfo
 rmance. Herbie Hancock\, winner of 14 Grammys\, portrayed one of the music
 ians and won an Oscar for the movie’s original score. Hancock also serve
 d as conductor and arranger for ’Round Midnight’s many jazz sequences.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/round-midnight-in-4-k
 -019be20f-3f2a-ec78-e260-05875ed0f9d5
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Scandal (Skyandaru) in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260415T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260415T213000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019c6888-2e89-ac69-0317-b2356a202baa@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Wednesday\, April 15\, 2026 at 8 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museu
 m of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 44m\n\n1950 | 104 min. | Japan | Black
 -and-White | Japanese with English subtitles | Not Rated | 35mm\nDIRECTED 
 BY: Akira Kurosawa  \nWRITTEN BY: Ryuko Kikushima\, Akira Kurosawa \nWITH
 : Toshiro Mifune\, Yoshiko Yamaguchi\, Takashi Shimura\, Yoko Katsuragi\nP
 rint courtesy of The Japan Foundation\, Los Angeles.\n\nType: Screenings\n
 \nReleased the same year as his celebrated Rashomon\, Kurosawa’s tenth d
 irectorial effort was made in response to the rise of sensational tabloid 
 journalism that paralleled Japan’s newfound concerns with freedom of spe
 ech. By crafting a story that follows two famous artists who sue a gossip 
 rag for insinuating their romantic involvement\, Kurosawa hoped that Scand
 al would spark such public outcry to the distasteful trend as to quash its
  popularity. As he noted in his 1982 memoir—and as evidenced with the la
 ter rise of reality television—“Scandal proved to be as ineffectual a 
 weapon against slander as a praying mantis against a hatchet.”
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/scandal-skyandaru-in-
 35-mm-019c6888-2e89-ac69-0317-b2356a202baa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rocco and His Brothers in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260417T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260417T163000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019be23a-24ef-b6ef-3eec-d23b9c1a1769@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, April 17\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museu
 m of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 59m\n\n1960 | 179 min. | Italy/France 
 | Black-and-White | Italian with English subtitles | Not Rated | 4K DCP  \
 nDIRECTED BY: Luchino Visconti  \nWRITTEN BY: Suso Cecchi D’Amico\, Pas
 quale Festa Campanile\, Massimo Franciosa\, Enrico Medioli\, Luchino Visco
 nti  \nSTORY BY: Luchino Visconti\, Suso Cecchi D’Amico\, Vasco Pratoli
 ni  \nWITH: Alain Delon\, Renato Salvatori\, Annie Girardot\, Katina Paxi
 nou\n\nType: Screenings\n\nRocco and His Brothers was a later discovery fo
 r Bong Joon Ho\, who put the film on his 2022 Sight and Sound list as one 
 of the 10 films he considers the greatest of all time. An epic melodrama f
 rom director Luchino Visconti\, the film helped to make an international s
 tar of French actor Alain Delon\, cast as one of five sons of a poor rural
  Italian family whose fortunes fall even further after a move to Milan. Th
 e screenplay was a collaboration between Visconti and four other writers\,
  including Suso Cecchi D’Amico—one of the first female screenwriters i
 n Italian cinema and a key figure in the neorealist movement\; her body of
  work includes such classics as Bicycle Thieves (1948).
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/rocco-and-his-brother
 s-019be23a-24ef-b6ef-3eec-d23b9c1a1769
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Idiot (Hakuchi) in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260417T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260417T210000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019c063e-b79c-6955-22cc-3cba2eaa5cf0@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: Anne McKnight\, associate professor of Japanese and
  comparative literature\n\nFriday\, April 17\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation
 : Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 46m\n\n1951 | 166 min. 
 | Japan | Black-and-White | Japanese with English subtitles | Not Rated | 
 35mm\nDIRECTED BY: Akira Kurosawa  \nWRITTEN BY: Eijiro Hisaita\, Akira K
 urosawa  \nWITH: Setsuko Hara\, Masayuki Mori\, Toshiro Mifune\, Yoshiko 
 Kuga \nPrint courtesy of The Japan Foundation\, Los Angeles.\n\nType: Scre
 enings\n\nBased on the 1869 novel by acclaimed Russian novelist Fyodor Dos
 toevsky\, Kurosawa updates the setting from Saint Petersburg to Hokkaido f
 or a story about “the destruction of a pure soul by a faithless world.
 ” Facing an original runtime of more than four hours\, the studio Shochi
 ku forced him to cut it down to less than three\, despite the director’s
  protests: “If you want to cut it\, you had better cut it lengthwise.”
  Shochiku won the battle\; Kurosawa left the studio. While the film was pa
 nned on its release in both Japan and America\, the director told Donald R
 ichie in 1990\, “One should be brave enough to risk this kind of ‘mist
 ake.’ Nowadays no one does.”
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-idiot-hakuchi-in-
 35-mm-019c063e-b79c-6955-22cc-3cba2eaa5cf0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Careers in Film Summit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260418T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260418T180000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019c6dd1-f08b-c9dd-086c-822ab4c5f7a5@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Conversations
DESCRIPTION:In person: Actors Jessica Alba and Keke Palmer\n\nA free annua
 l program that raises awareness about film industry jobs for high-school a
 nd college students\, and others from under-resourced communities.\n\nSatu
 rday\, April 18\, 2026 at 10 am\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pict
 ures\n\nType: Conversations\n\nMark your calendars and join the Academy Mu
 seum on April 18 for the 2026 Careers in Film Summit\, a free annual progr
 am that raises awareness about film industry jobs for high-school and coll
 ege students\, and others from under-resourced communities. Each moderated
  panel includes live Q&As with Academy members and other industry professi
 onals. \nEnjoy demonstrations\, workshops\, complimentary professional hea
 dshots\, and free entry to museum galleries with a summit ticket. American
  Sign Language (ASL) interpretation is available. \nThis year\, the Academ
 y Museum welcomes actor Jessica Alba as a special guest.\nSchedule*\n10am 
 | Museum opens \n10:30am–11:15am | Welcome remarks and keynote address w
 ith Jessica Alba | Ted Mann Theater \n11:15am–4pm | Las Fotos Project po
 rtraits | Sidney Poitier Grand Lobby\nCome camera-ready and get a complime
 ntary\, professional headshot.\n11:30am–2pm | On set with the Academy Mu
 seum | Tea Room (5th Floor) \nDrop by\, go on set with the Academy Museum\
 , and discover key careers in filmmaking. Learn about on-set jobs\; experi
 ment with professional equipment\; and interact with a sample production s
 et.\n11:30am and 12:30pm | Industry insights | SoC 1\nStudents can speak d
 irectly with professionals\, fielding industry insights\, tips\, and advic
 e\, and getting their questions answered. Space is limited. Program is fir
 st come\, first served.\n       Session 1 | 11:30am–12:15pm\n       Sess
 ion 2 | 12:30–1:15pm\n12:30 and 2:30pm | Voice and sound workshops | Shi
 rley Temple Education Studio \nArtists share knowledge about their career 
 paths followed by voice acting and sound designs demonstration. Space is l
 imited. Program is first come\, first served.\n12:30pm–1:30pm – Voice 
 acting with Bob Bergen (current voice of Porky Pig) \n2:30pm–3:30pm – 
 The art of Foley \n4–4:30pm | Keynote conversation with Keke Palmer  | T
 ed Mann Theater \nGain firsthand knowledge of working in the industry with
  a discussion on finding your voice and identifying key skills for your ca
 reer.\n5–6pm | Lights\, camera\, action! with Antigravity Academy | Ted 
 Mann Theater \nThere is so much that goes into making a film that we don't
  see onscreen. Join Academy Award-nominated director Carlos López Estrada
 \, whose films include Dìdi (2024)\, Raya and the Last Dragon (2021)\, Bl
 indspotting (2018) and founder of Antigravity Academy\, a multi-hyphenate 
 creative home for emerging artists across mediums\, as he explores careers
  in film with a panel of industry professionals. \n6-7pm | Coffee and care
 er mixer | TMT Lobby\nMeet Academy Members\, industry professionals and me
 mbers of community organizations\, and career opportunities they may have 
 to share. Light refreshment will be available.\n6pm | Museum closes \nPLEA
 SE NOTE: All summit participants\, and their guardians if participants are
  under the age of 18\, understand that the Academy Museum has the right to
  photograph and film any participation in the summit. All photography and 
 videography will be wide-angle in nature and used solely in connection wit
 h highlighting the summit on the Academy Museum website\, YouTube\, and so
 cial media channels.\nSummit tickets are available on a first-come\, first
 -served basis and do not guarantee seating in the Ted Mann Theater\, SoC 1
  or access to the Shirley Temple Education Studio sessions.\n* Program par
 ticipants and programs are subject to change.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/2026-careers-in-film-
 summit-019c6dd1-f08b-c9dd-086c-822ab4c5f7a5
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:I Live in Fear (Ikimono no kiroku) in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260418T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260418T203000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019c064a-bcdc-fe1d-37a2-55f3614fb0bb@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, April 18\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 43m\n\n1955 | 103 min. | Japan | Bla
 ck-and-White | Japanese with English subtitles | Not Rated | 35mm\nDIRECTE
 D BY: Akira Kurosawa \nWRITTEN BY: Akira Kurosawa\, Shinobu Hashimoto\, Hi
 deo Oguni \nWITH: Toshiro Mifune\, Takashi Shimura\, Minoru Chiaki\, Masa
 o Shimizu\n\nType: Screenings\n\nKurosawa contemplates the horrors of the 
 atomic bomb and the fear that permeated postwar Japan in this 1955 drama. 
 Kiichi (Toshiro Mifune)\, an aging industrialist who owns a foundry\, slow
 ly loses his grip on reality as his fear of nuclear annihilation leads him
  to work toward relocating his family to Brazil. Alarmed by his paranoias\
 , the family attempts to have him declared legally incompetent. I Live in 
 Fear is a bleak\, cautionary tale that explores dissonance of reality and 
 delusion\, driven by collective anxiety and instigated by isolation.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/i-live-in-fear-in-35-
 mm-019c064a-bcdc-fe1d-37a2-55f3614fb0bb
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Midnight Cowboy in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260419T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260419T160000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019be226-d097-65cf-a70e-af6a6dd5561f@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, April 19\, 2026 at 2 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum o
 f Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 53m\n\n1969 | 113 min. | USA | Color | En
 glish | Rated R | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: John Schlesinger \nWRITTEN BY: Wal
 do Salt \nWITH: Dustin Hoffman\, Jon Voight\, Sylvia Miles\, Jon McGiver\n
 \nType: Screenings\n\nDirector John Schlesinger’s film version of James 
 Leo Herlihy’s novel about two unlikely friends—a would-be gigolo and a
  petty hustler—in the seedier side of 1960s Manhattan was a breakthrough
  in American cinema’s treatment of previously taboo subject matter. \nBe
 st Actor nominations were earned by Dustin Hoffman as the ailing “Ratso
 ” Rizzo and Jon Voight in a star-making turn as Joe Buck\, with supporti
 ng actress nominee Sylvia Miles among the impressive cast assembled by Sch
 lesinger and pioneering\, uncredited casting director Marion Dougherty. Th
 e film earned Oscars for Best Picture (Jerome Hellman\, producer)\, Schles
 inger’s direction\, and Waldo Salt’s screenplay.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/midnight-cowboy-019be
 226-d097-65cf-a70e-af6a6dd5561f
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:One Wonderful Sunday (Subarashiki nichiyobi) in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260419T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260419T160000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019c068d-fb79-8423-d71b-7307313ee163@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: Academy Collection and Preservation Executive Vice 
 President Matt Severson\n\nSunday\, April 19\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation
 : Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 48m\n\n1947 | 108 min. 
 | Japan | Black-and-White | Japanese with English subtitles | Not Rated | 
 35mm\nDIRECTED BY: Akira Kurosawa  \nWRITTEN BY: Akira Kurosawa\, Keinosu
 ke Uekusa  \nWITH: Isao Numasaki\, Chieko Nakakita\, Atsushi Watanabe\, Z
 ekô Nakamura\nPrint courtesy of The Japan Foundation\, Los Angeles.\n\nTy
 pe: Screenings\n\nEngaged couple Yuzo and Masako take a weekend trip to To
 kyo\, a city recently devastated by World War II\, with little more than 3
 5 yen—approximately $1—and the goal of having a great time. Employing 
 sequences of fantasy via the couple’s imagination\, One Wonderful Sunday
  is the most hopeful film from Akira Kurosawa’s early period. His fascin
 ation with dream life\, seen in his later Dreams (1990\, screening May 29)
 \, first emerges in this poignant\, romantic\, and hopeful vision of the f
 uture\, which was shot entirely on location using hidden cameras with two 
 unknown actors. The film earned Kurosawa a prize for directing at the Main
 ichi Film Awards\, which he would later also receive for Kagemusha (1980) 
 and Ran (1985).
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/one-wonderful-sunday-
 subarashiki-nichiyobi-in-35-mm-019c068d-fb79-8423-d71b-7307313ee163
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Lower Depths (Donzoko) in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260419T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260419T203000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019c064b-5bcb-9df8-5424-65decc456d57@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, April 19\, 2026 at 6:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museu
 m of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 5m\n\n1957 | 125 min. | Japan | Black-
 and-White | Japanese with English subtitles | Not Rated | 35mm\nDIRECTED B
 Y: Akira Kurosawa\nWRITTEN BY: Akira Kurosawa\, Hideo Oguni. \nWITH: Toshi
 ro Mifune\, Isuzu Yamada\, Kyoko Kagawa\, Ganjiro Nakamura\n\nType: Screen
 ings\n\nKurosawa takes a picaresque approach in his adaptation of Maxim Go
 rky’s play of the same name from 1902\, with a twist of humor and joy in
  underlying despair—the premise of the work. Set in the late Edo period\
 , the film surveys the lives of a married couple and their tenants who are
  barely scraping by in a run-down tenement. Kurosawa uses the limited spac
 e of the tenement to create an intimate atmosphere for the ensemble to per
 form in with density that\, in turn\, resembles the anguish that each char
 acter carries within them.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-lower-depths-in-3
 5-mm-019c064b-5bcb-9df8-5424-65decc456d57
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Servant in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260420T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260420T163000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019be23a-9e3f-b3b3-c986-549b2fe9d4cb@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, April 20\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museu
 m of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 56m\n\n1963 | 116 min. | UK | Black-an
 d-White | English | Not Rated | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Joseph Losey  \nWRI
 TTEN BY: Harold Pinter  \nWITH: Dirk Bogarde\, James Fox\, Sarah Miles\, 
 Wendy Craig\n\nType: Screenings\n\nDirector Joseph Losey’s first of thre
 e collaborations with writer Harold Pinter was this adaptation of Robin Ma
 ugham’s 1948 novella. Focusing on social class and interpersonal relatio
 nships\, the story follows Barrett (Dirk Bogarde) who is hired as manserva
 nt when the wealthy Tony (James Fox) moves into a new house. The two form 
 a bond\, but Tony is unaware of Barrett’s ulterior motive to gain the up
 per hand in their relationship. To further his goals\, Barrett convinces T
 ony to hire a maid and brings his lover (Sara Miles) into the home under t
 he guise that they are siblings.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-servant-in-4-k-01
 9be23a-9e3f-b3b3-c986-549b2fe9d4cb
END:VEVENT
