BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Warriors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260422T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260422T223000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019be20f-917c-acf5-abc9-3c4c810fae88@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: producer Lawrence Gordon \nSelected by the Producer
 s Branch\n\nWednesday\, April 22\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mu
 seum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 34m\n\n1979 | 94 min. | USA | Color
  | English | Rated R | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Walter Hill \nWRITTEN BY: David 
 Shaber\, Walter Hill \nWITH: Michael Beck\, James Remar\, Deborah Van Valk
 enburgh\, Marcelino Sanchez\n\nType: Screenings\n\nDirector Walter Hill’
 s action classic focuses on street toughs framed for the murder of a chari
 smatic gang leader and forced to flee to their Coney Island neighborhood. 
 Working from a shrewdly minimalist script adapted by Hill and David Shaber
  from the novel by Sol Yurick\, Hill and producer Lawrence Gordon (their o
 ther collaborations include 48 Hrs.\, 1982\, and Streets of Fire\, 1984) c
 reated a stylized vision of 1970s New York that remains one of the directo
 r’s most popular and influential films.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-warriors-019be20f
 -917c-acf5-abc9-3c4c810fae88
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Hidden Fortress (Kakushi toride no san-akunin) in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260423T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260423T203000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019c064c-8eb1-23fa-9df5-1a936093f4b2@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, April 23\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 6m\n\n1958 | 126 min. | Japan | Blac
 k-and-White | Japanese with English subtitles | Not Rated | 35mm \nDIRECTE
 D BY: Akira Kurosawa \nWRITTEN BY: Ryuzo Kikushima\, Hideo Oguni\, Shinobu
  Hashimoto\, Akira Kurosawa\nWITH: Toshiro Mifune\, Misa Uehara\, Minoru C
 hiaki\, Kamatari Fujiwara\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA pair of hapless peasant
 s—Tahei (Minoru Chiaki) and Matashichi (Kamatari Fujiwara)—uproot thei
 r lives to enlist with the rising Yamana clan. But their witless greed kee
 ps landing them in unfortunate circumstances. Their ingenious plan to esca
 pe into a neighboring state draws the attention of General Rokurota Makabe
  (Toshiro Mifune). Hiding in disguise with Princess Yuki (Misa Uehara) of 
 the fallen Akizuki clan\, Makabe enlists the help of Tahei and Matashichi 
 for passage into Hayakawa. This 16th-century period adventure of a princes
 s evading capture from enemy forces served as inspiration for George Lucas
 ’s space epic\, Star Wars (1977).
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-hidden-fortress-i
 n-35-mm-019c064c-8eb1-23fa-9df5-1a936093f4b2
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gallery Spotlight: Screenwriting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T130000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019d0c5c-c749-769e-32d2-72f659590c47@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Conversations
DESCRIPTION:Academy members and screenwriters reveal the nuances of bringi
 ng stories to the screen.\n\nFriday\, April 24\, 2026 at 12 pm\n\nLocation
 : Ted Mann Theater Lobby\n\nType: Conversations\n\nA screenplay is a writt
 en document that establishes the foundation of a film\, providing its dial
 ogue\, setting\, and action\, and dictating its structure and story. But i
 t is more than a blueprint\; it is an art form. \nAcademy governors and sc
 reenwriters Howard A. Rodman (August\, 2008)\, and Dana Stevens (The Woman
  King\, 2022)\, reveal the unique nuances of writing for films against the
  backdrop of our new gallery\, Screenwriting: Takes on LA Noir. \nAssistan
 t Curator Nicholas Barlow moderates. \nAbout Gallery SpotlightsGallery Spo
 tlights feature special guests who bring fresh insights to our exhibitions
 . Join us for revealing monthly conversations connecting the objects in ou
 r galleries to the art and history of moviemaking.\nIf you have any questi
 ons or need assistance planning your visit\, please email museumeducation@
 oscars.org.
LOCATION:Ted Mann Theater Lobby
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/gallery-spotlight-scr
 eenwriting-019d0c5c-c749-769e-32d2-72f659590c47
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Servant in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T163000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019be23a-f640-8c01-dff2-d41b5ca36a8b@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, April 24\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museu
 m of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 56m\n\n1963 | 116 min. | UK | Black-an
 d-White | English | Not Rated | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Joseph Losey  \nWRI
 TTEN BY: Harold Pinter  \nWITH: Dirk Bogarde\, James Fox\, Sarah Miles\, 
 Wendy Craig\n\nType: Screenings\n\nDirector Joseph Losey’s first of thre
 e collaborations with writer Harold Pinter was this adaptation of Robin Ma
 ugham’s 1948 novella. Focusing on social class and interpersonal relatio
 nships\, the story follows Barrett (Dirk Bogarde) who is hired as manserva
 nt when the wealthy Tony (James Fox) moves into a new house. The two form 
 a bond\, but Tony is unaware of Barrett’s ulterior motive to gain the up
 per hand in their relationship. To further his goals\, Barrett convinces T
 ony to hire a maid and brings his lover (Sara Miles) into the home under t
 he guise that they are siblings.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-servant-in-4-k-01
 9be23a-f640-8c01-dff2-d41b5ca36a8b
