SUMMARY:The Wind Rises
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T121500
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019be21f-0b8a-b426-a322-7ddbd1f4d76b@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Accessible screening\n\nSaturday\, April 25\, 2026 at 11 am\n\
 nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 6m\n\n2013 | 1
 26 min. | Japan | Color | English (Dubbed) | Rated PG-13 | DCP\nDIRECTED/W
 RITTEN BY: Hayao Miyazaki\nWITH: Joseph Gordon-Levitt\, John Krasinski\, E
 mily Blunt\, Martin Short\n\nType: Screenings\n\nAccessible screeningOn th
 e last Saturday of every month\, the museum's Family Matinee is an accommo
 dative screening where we offer open captioning\, keep the theater dimly l
 it\, and maintain a lower volume specifically for neurodivergent viewers. 
 \nHayao Miyazaki’s Oscar-nominated feature is a novelistic\, historical 
 drama that unfolds over decades. Inspired by the famous Italian aeronautic
 al designer Gianni Caproni\, Jiro dreams of designing and flying beautiful
  airplanes. Nearsighted and thus unable to be a pilot\, Jiro instead becom
 es one of the world’s most accomplished airplane designers. As war looms
 \, he finds his work transitioning from creating graceful flying machines 
 to deadly tools of destruction. Interlaced with an epic romance\, The Wind
  Rises is a mature work from a master.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-wind-rises-019be2
 1f-0b8a-b426-a322-7ddbd1f4d76b
END:VEVENT
