SUMMARY:Inside Jaws: The Art of Cinematography with Dion Beebe
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T150000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019c3574-120c-abbc-c0c1-6ee685dcd44b@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Conversations
DESCRIPTION:How did the makers of Jaws achieve so many iconic shots? Learn
  about the art and science of film photography with Academy member and cin
 ematographer Dion Beebe.\n\nSaturday\, April 25\, 2026 at 2 pm\n\nLocation
 : Level 4\n\nCost: Free with general admission\n\nType: Conversations\n\nC
 inematographer and Academy member Dion Beebe gives a 30-minute tour highli
 ghting the art of motion picture photography. Learn about the technical nu
 ances cinematographers consider\, including camera choice\, and how so man
 y iconic shots from Jaws (1975) came together under the expertise of Bill 
 Butler and his team.   \nStay for a brief Q&A with Beebe after the tour
 .
LOCATION:Level 4
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/inside-jaws-the-art-o
 f-cinematography-with-dion-beebe-019c3574-120c-abbc-c0c1-6ee685dcd44b
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Man for All Seasons in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T163000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019be271-3c35-eff7-ac05-d99ee9f001cb@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, April 25\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h\n\n1966 | 120 min. | UK | Color | En
 glish | Rated G | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Fred Zinnemann \nWRITTEN BY: Robe
 rt Bolt \nWITH: Wendy Hiller\, Leo McKern\, Robert Shaw\, Paul Scofield\n\
 nType: Screenings\n\nRobert Bolt’s adaptation of his own Tony Award–wi
 nning play tells the inspiring true story of Thomas More\, the Lord Chance
 llor of England\, who risked his life in defying the will of King Henry VI
 II\, who demanded the church’s permission to divorce his first wife in o
 rder to marry Anne Boleyn. \nThe film won Oscars for Best Picture\, Direct
 ing (both for producer-director Fred Zinnemann)\, Bolt’s screenplay\, Pa
 ul Scofield’s performance as More\, and the film’s color cinematograph
 y and costume design. Oscar winner Wendy Hiller (Separate Tables\, 1958) w
 as nominated for her touching performance as More’s wife\, and Robert Sh
 aw earned his only nomination for his charismatic performance as the mercu
 rial Henry\, commanding the screen with only a few scenes.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/a-man-for-all-seasons
 -019be271-3c35-eff7-ac05-d99ee9f001cb
