SUMMARY:La La Land in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260429T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260429T223000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019be20f-d475-f66e-00fb-868248073bbe@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: choreographer Mandy Moore\, music supervisor ​Ste
 ven Gizicki and stunt coordinator Mark Kubr\nSelected by the Production an
 d Technology Branch\n\nWednesday\, April 29\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation:
  Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 8m\n\n2016 | 128 min. | 
 USA | Color | Scope | English | Rated PG-13 | 35mm \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: 
 Damien Chazelle \nWITH: Ryan Gosling\, Emma Stone\, John Legend\, Rosemari
 e DeWitt \nPrint courtesy of the Academy Film Archive.\n\nType: Screenings
 \n\nThis stylish\, old-fashioned musical about two young Angelenos in love
  was one of the most pleasant cinematic surprises of 2016. Best Actor nomi
 nee Ryan Gosling plays the jazz musician whose love for aspiring actress E
 mma Stone (who won her first Best Actress Oscar for her performance) may n
 ot be enough to withstand the challenges of their ambitions. \nThe film is
  one of three to earn a then-record 14 nominations—including Best Pictur
 e—and it won Oscars for its cinematography\, original score\, original s
 ong “City of Stars\,” production design\, and Damien Chazelle’s dire
 ction. Chazelle and his team staged elaborate song-and-dance numbers on lo
 cation around Los Angeles\, some in lengthy\, unbroken takes.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/la-la-land-019be20f-d
 475-f66e-00fb-868248073bbe
END:VEVENT
