SUMMARY:The Taking of Pelham One Two Three in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T160000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019c0c85-2c76-b048-af19-337f7260369b@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, May 2\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 44m\n\n1974 | 104 min. | USA | Color | 
 Scope | English | Rated R | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Joseph Sargent \nWRITTEN B
 Y: Peter Stone \nWITH: Walter Matthau\, Robert Shaw\, Martin Balsam\, Hect
 or Elizondo\n\nType: Screenings\n\nFour armed men hijack a subway car on a
  sweltering Manhattan day in this witty thriller adapted by Peter Stone (C
 harade\, 1963) from the bestseller by John Godey. Walter Matthau is the cy
 nical transit cop who must negotiate with the hostage-takers\, led by a su
 btly menacing Robert Shaw as an ex-mercenary. \nExpertly directed by Josep
 h Sargent (Colossus: The Forbin Project\, 1970)\, this classic from the Fu
 n City era of New York features gritty wide-screen cinematography by five-
 time Academy Award nominee and Honorary Award winner Owen Roizman (The Fre
 nch Connection\, 1971) and a brassy and percussive score by Oscar winner D
 avid Shire (Norma Rae\, 1979).
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/taking-of-pelham-one-
 two-three-019c0c85-2c76-b048-af19-337f7260369b
