BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening of Short Films from Asian American Filmmakers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T223000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019be210-a94b-d065-dfac-b8b273f32904@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Wednesday\, May 13\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 6m\n\nBead Game \n1977 | 6 min. | Canada
  | Color | English \nDIRECTED BY: Ishu Patel \nSoar \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY:
  Alyce Tzue \n2014 | 7 min. | USA | Color | English \nWITH: Shira Abergel\
 , Mason Welch \nSewing Woman \n1982 | 14 min. | USA | Black-and-White | En
 glish\nDIRECTED BY: Arthur Dong \nWRITTEN BY: Lorraine Dong \nWITH: Lisa L
 u \nNai Nai & Wài Pó \n2023 | 17 min. | USA | Color | English\, Mandarin
  \nDIRECTED BY: Sean Wang \nGwai Lo: The Little Foreigner \n2002 | 12 min.
  | USA | Color | English \nDIRECTED BY: Jon M. Chu \nDol (First Birthday) 
 \n2011 | 12 min. | USA | Color | English \nDIRECTED/WRITEN BY: Andrew Ahn 
 \nWITH: Muki Grossberg\, Joshua Kwak\, James S.W. Lee\, Martin Lee \nNami 
 \n2015 | 13 min. | USA | Color | English \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Masami Kaw
 ai \nWITH: Kana Kawai \nWinning in America \n2021 | 10 min. | USA | Color 
 | English \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Amrita Singh \nWITH: Rithika Tudmilla\, R
 anjan Singh\, Shiney Simon\, Rahul Tudmilla\n\nType: Screenings\n\nThe Aca
 demy is celebrating Asian American\, Native American\, and Pacific Islande
 r Heritage month with this selection of short films featuring Asian Americ
 an filmmakers and stories. The evening includes two animated films\, Ishu 
 Patel’s Oscar-nominated Bead Game (1977)\, and Soar (2014)\, from filmma
 ker Alyce Tzue. Arthur Dong’s Oscar-nominated documentary short\, Sewing
  Woman (1982)\, tells the life story of the filmmaker’s mother\, while S
 ean Wang (Dìdi) was nominated for his documentary Nai Nai & Wài Pó (202
 3)\, depicting the close friendship of his elderly grandmothers. Jon M. Ch
 u (Wicked\, 2024) won a DGA Student Film Award for his musical short Gwai 
 Lo: The Little Foreigner (2002). Filmmaker Andrew Ahn (Fire Island\, 2022)
  made his short film Dol (First Birthday\, 2011) partly as a way of coming
  out to his parents. Masami Kawai’s Nami (2015) depicts a day in the lif
 e of a grieving widow in her journey across Los Angeles. In Amrita Singh
 ’s Winning in America (2021)\, a teenage girl faces the challenges of a 
 spelling bee and her coach father.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/an-evening-of-short-f
 ilms-from-asian-american-filmmakers-019be210-a94b-d065-dfac-b8b273f32904
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Night and the City in 35mm nitrate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260514T203000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019c0651-3856-5dfc-6db8-c395e72fb72a@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, May 14\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museu
 m of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 36m\n\n1950 | 96 min. | UK/USA | Black
 -and-White | English | Not Rated | 35mm nitrate \nDIRECTED BY: Jules Dassi
 n\nWRITTEN BY: Jo Eisinger\nWITH: Richard Widmark\, Gene Tierney\, Googie 
 Withers\, Hugh Marlowe \n35mm nitrate collection print courtesy of the UCL
 A Film & Television Archive.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nAmerican director Jule
 s Dassin’s British noir follows Harry (Richard Widmark)\, a small-time h
 ustler dreaming of dominating the wrestling racket. When he double-crosses
  London’s underworld\, his lies become a death warrant in the city’s m
 erciless alleys.\nShot in the UK while Dassin was fleeing persecution and 
 the Hollywood blacklist\, Night and the City is the first of several films
  he made abroad in Britain\, France\, and Greece. This rare original nitra
 te print is of the British release version of the film\, which runs six mi
 nutes longer than the US release and features alternate opening and closin
 g scenes as well as a score by prolific British composer Benjamin Frankel.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/night-and-the-city-in
 -35-mm-nitrate-019c0651-3856-5dfc-6db8-c395e72fb72a
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Community Conversation: Representation in Animation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260515T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260515T130000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019d2732-52a9-a9c4-1341-06b9de4cac7b@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Conversations
DESCRIPTION:Angela Sanchez of LatinX in Animation and Austin Faber of Blac
 k N’ Animated discuss the past\, present\, and future of their communiti
 es’ voices in animated film.\n\nFriday\, May 15\, 2026 at 12 pm\n\nLocat
 ion: Sidney Poitier Grand Lobby\n\nType: Conversations\n\nLatinX in Animat
 ion Development and Strategy Consultant Angela Sanchez and Black N’ Anim
 ated Director Austin Faber discuss the portrayal of their communities in a
 nimated films throughout history\; the significance of authentic represent
 ation in animation\; how to support animators of color\, and more.
LOCATION:Sidney Poitier Grand Lobby
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/community-conversatio
 n-representation-in-animation-019d2732-52a9-a9c4-1341-06b9de4cac7b
END:VEVENT
