BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Being There in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T223000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019be210-d889-23c4-fc46-fb61ed623eb5@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Selected by the Sound Branch\n\nWednesday\, May 20\, 2026 at 7
 :30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 10m\n
 \n1979 | 130 min. | USA/West Germany | Color | English | Rated PG | 35mm \
 nDIRECTED BY: Hal Ashby \nWRITTEN BY: Jerzy Kosinski \nWITH: Peter Sellers
 \, Shirley MacLaine\, Jack Warden\, Melvyn Douglas\n\nType: Screenings\n\n
 Hal Ashby directed this satirical comedy-drama\, adapted by Jerzy Kosinski
  from his own novel\, about a sheltered gardener of little intellect (Best
  Actor nominee Peter Sellers\, in a subtle and remarkable comic performanc
 e) who finds himself among Washington\, DC\, power brokers who interpret h
 is every befuddled utterance as great wisdom.\nOscar winner Johnny Mandel 
 (The Sandpiper\, 1965) composed the film’s Satie-esque score. Expert sou
 nd for this dialogue-driven story\, which contrasts the harsh noises of ur
 ban life with the hushed halls of power\, was the work of Oscar-nominated 
 production sound mixer Jeff Wexler and Oscar-winning re-recording mixer Do
 nald O. Mitchell. Melvyn Douglas won his second Supporting Actor Oscar for
  his moving performance as the tycoon Benjamin Rand.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/being-there-019be210-
 d889-23c4-fc46-fb61ed623eb5
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Hidden Room (aka Obsession)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260521T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260521T203000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019c065b-dc76-64a4-0aea-86ab36464280@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, May 21\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museu
 m of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 36m\n\n1949 | 96 min. | UK | Black-and
 -White | English | Not Rated | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Edward Dmytryk\nWRITTEN/
 BASED ON A NOVEL BY: Alec Coppel\nWITH: Robert Newton\, Sally Gray\, Naunt
 on Wayne\, Phil Brown\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA London psychiatrist (Robert
  Newton\, Around the World in 80 Days\, 1956) smuggles acid from work dail
 y to a blitzed building\, with the aim of killing and dissolving the body 
 of his wife’s American lover (Phil Brown\, best known as Uncle Owen in S
 tar Wars Episode IV: A New Hope\, 1977). Featuring a stirring score by Ita
 lian composer Nino Rota (The Godfather\, 1972)\, this slow-burn relationsh
 ip drama turns into a thrilling game of cat-and-mouse once Scotland Yard s
 ets its sights on the missing American. Feverishly directed by blacklisted
 \, Oscar-nominated Edward Dmytryk (Crossfire\, 1947)\, this story is truly
  where Kafka meets film noir.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-hidden-room-aka-o
 bsession-019c065b-dc76-64a4-0aea-86ab36464280
END:VEVENT
