BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Boy and the Heron
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T121500
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019be220-9c0e-c24b-a8ce-9d4d515e0c35@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Accessible screening\n\nSaturday\, May 30\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nL
 ocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 4m\n\n2023 | 124
  min. | Japan | Color | English (Dubbed) | Rated PG-13 | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRI
 TTEN BY: Hayao Miyazaki\nWITH: Luca Padovan\, Robert Pattinson\, Christian
  Bale\, Gemma Chan\, Dave Bautista\n\nType: Screenings\n\nHayao Miyazaki
 ’s latest Oscar-winning feature is also his most autobiographical\, insp
 ired by Genzaburo Yoshino’s 1937 novel How Do You Live? (which is the Ja
 panese title for the film)\, and the effect World War II had on Miyazaki's
  childhood. The result is one of Miyazaki’s darkest and most mature film
 s. After losing his mother during the war\, Mahito and his father move to 
 the countryside for a fresh start. Still haunted by this loss and the rece
 nt disappearance of his new stepmom\, Mahito is lured to an ancient tower 
 by a gray heron and ends up in a world where the distinction between the l
 iving and the dead disappears. Guided by the heron\, he must battle his gr
 ief and learn that he has the capability to create a better world.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-boy-and-the-heron
 -019be220-9c0e-c24b-a8ce-9d4d515e0c35
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Deep in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T160000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019c0662-8062-5739-9390-cffa085d0882@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, May 30\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museu
 m of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 4m\n\n1977 | 124 min. | USA | Color | 
 Scope | English | Rated PG | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Peter Yates \nWRITTEN BY:
  Peter Benchley\, Tracy Keenan Wynn \nWITH: Robert Shaw\, Jacqueline Bisse
 t\, Nick Nolte\, Eli Wallach\n\nType: Screenings\n\nThe bestselling aquati
 c thriller by Jaws author Peter Benchley became a summer blockbuster under
  the direction of four-time Oscar nominee Peter Yates (Bullitt\, 1968)\, w
 ith Robert Shaw commanding the screen as a Bahamas treasure hunter who aid
 s a vacationing couple (Jacqueline Bisset and Nick Nolte) in a dangerous h
 unt for a sunken fortune. \nThe film’s memorable diving scenes benefit f
 rom the impressive underwater cinematography of second unit directors Al G
 iddings (The Abyss\, 1989) and Stan Waterman\, and the evocative score by 
 five-time Oscar winner John Barry.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-deep-in-35-mm-019
 c0662-8062-5739-9390-cffa085d0882
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Madadayo (No\, Not Yet!) in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T213000
DTSTAMP:20260401T083316Z
UID:019c0663-453c-82a2-5032-4355b581436b@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, May 30\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museu
 m of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 14m\n\n1993 | 134 min. | Japan | Color
  | Japanese with English subtitles | Not Rated | 35mm\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY
 : Akira Kurosawa \nWITH: Tatsuo Matsumura\, Kyoko Kagawa\, Hisashi Igawa\,
  George Tokoro\nPrint courtesy of The Japan Foundation\, Los Angeles.\n\nT
 ype: Screenings\n\nThe 50-year career of one of history’s greatest filmm
 akers concludes with this heartwarming finale from 1993\, dedicated to cel
 ebrated and respected writer and educator Hyakken Uchida. After Uchida ann
 ounces his retirement from teaching\, his students host an annual gatherin
 g\, the “Not Yet Banquet” to celebrate his life and career. Composed o
 f a series of poignant episodes\, Kurosawa invites us into a world where b
 eauty can be found\, despite the inevitable pitfalls of reality\, in genui
 ne connection\, loyalty\, and respect for all living creatures.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/madadayo-019c0663-453
 c-82a2-5032-4355b581436b
END:VEVENT
